<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21064] osc: max_cached_mb LRU counts one slot per cl_page, undercounts large folios</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21064</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The client osc LRU (max_cached_mb, osc_lru_alloc(), osc_lru_del(), osc_lru_add_batch(), osc_lru_shrink() in lustre/osc/osc_page.c) accounts one slot per cl_page. With large folio support (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19895" title="implement large folio support" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19895"&gt;LU-19895&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/65094" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65094&lt;/a&gt;) one cl_page can cover a folio of many base pages (cp_npgs), so a large folio takes a single LRU slot whatever its size. Cached base pages can then exceed max_cached_mb by up to the folio size per page, for written folios as well as readahead folios (readahead ra_cur_pages is already accounted in base pages and returns folio_nr_pages() on read completion).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is to count LRU slots in base pages (cp_npgs) in all the osc LRU counters and in the LRU shrink/reclaim paths, with tests that fill max_cached_mb using large folios.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found while reviewing change 65094 (thread on lustre/llite/rw.c, readahead folio accounting), where Andreas Dilger asked for this as a follow-on to that patch.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
